The empty result for `DDDDDD` doesn't prove the line isn't logged. I searched `textPayload`, but I believe the Ops Agent stores unparsed lines in `jsonPayload.message`. I haven't confirmed that. Run these two, which print only timestamps and no values:
```bash
gcloud logging read "logName=\"projects/$P/logs/backend_pm2_out\" AND jsonPayload.message:*" --project=$P --freshness=30m --limit=1 --format="value(timestamp)"
gcloud logging read "logName=\"projects/$P/logs/backend_pm2_out\" AND jsonPayload.message:\"DDDDDD\"" --project=$P --freshness=30m --limit=1 --format="value(timestamp)"
```
- The first printing a timestamp confirms the field.
